From 14413067bd607fde12b099d9836dae3c07f145d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexis Williams <alexis@typedr.at>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:26:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/24] Build the tests on Emscripten

The tests' meson files treat every non-Windows host as Unix, while the
library build excludes the Unix sources on Emscripten, so configuring
with -Dtests=true fails and several tests don't link.

Skip what Emscripten can't build:
- the Unix-only test blocks and programs in glib/tests and gio/tests,
  GIO_LAUNCH_DESKTOP, the dbus-launch helper and the gio-unix-2.0
  pkg-config test;
- the constructor test, whose shared libraries Meson can't link here;
- tests/lib's glibconfig.py, which only girepository's tests read;
- appmonitor (GDesktopAppInfo), gsubprocess (spawning) and unix-fd
  (fd passing), which test features Emscripten doesn't have;
- dynamictype and dynamictests: G_DEFINE_DYNAMIC_TYPE_EXTENDED refers
  to a type_name##_init_adapter that it never defines on WebAssembly.

In the tests that do build, exclude the subtests that call the
glib-unix and gio-unix APIs (mainloop, closure, pollable, the testing
stdin subtest), use pipe() where a test only needs a pipe
(spawn-singlethread, test-printf), skip the CPU affinity subtest
(Emscripten declares pthread_getaffinity_np but doesn't define it), and
give param's instance_init the class data argument it takes here.

WebAssembly traps on any call through a function pointer of another
type, so test code that registers callbacks with the wrong signature
now passes functions of the right type: class, instance and interface
init functions take their data argument, notify handlers their user
data, and small wrappers stand in where a test passed a library
function (g_strdup, g_free, g_usleep, g_main_loop_quit,
g_cancellable_cancel, g_object_unref) or one of its own functions
through another callback type. hook's hooks swap functions between
g_hook_list_invoke() and g_hook_list_invoke_check(), which call them
through different types.

The tool tests' runner looks for <tool>.js and runs it with the Node
that _G_TEST_PROGRAM_RUNNER_NODE names, which the meson files set on
Emscripten.

Only test sources and test build files change.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Wasm-specific]
